# Every text file is checked out with LF endings, on every OS.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with git's default core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# every script to CRLF, and a CRLF shebang (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`) fails with
# "bad interpreter" -- inside WSL too, when the clone was made from Windows.
# lib/tests/test_gitattributes.py pins it.
* text=auto eol=lf
